    <section class="section">
      <div class="shell">
        <div class="section-head center"><div class="section-kicker">A simple buying path</div><h2 class="section-title">Diagnose before you build.</h2></div>
        <div class="four-grid">
          <article class="step-card"><span class="step-number">1</span><h3>Run the check</h3><p>Get a directional indication without paying for analysis.</p></article>
          <article class="step-card"><span class="step-number">2</span><h3>Let VizAI prepare</h3><p>VizAI performs the research, analysis, structuring, and drafting within the defined service scope.</p></article>
          <article class="step-card"><span class="step-number">3</span><h3>Confirm and approve</h3><p>The customer confirms facts; VizAI reviews quality and approves the deliverable or action.</p></article>
          <article class="step-card"><span class="step-number">4</span><h3>Maintain what matters</h3><p>VizAI executes the cadence while decisions and exceptions continue through human gates.</p></article>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="section dark">
      <div class="shell">
        <div class="section-head"><div class="section-kicker">Maintenance scope</div><h2 class="section-title">Recurring work has explicit boundaries.</h2><p class="section-copy">The baseline plan includes one monthly fact-change request, up to five factual changes, one small infrastructure correction, and a defined monthly monitoring set. Larger work is estimated separately.</p></div>
        <div class="maintenance-loop">
          <div class="loop-step"><span>Weekly</span><strong>Technical validation</strong><p>Check hosted profile and record integrity.</p></div>
          <div class="loop-step"><span>Monthly</span><strong>Monitoring set</strong><p>Run the agreed systems, prompts, and observations.</p></div>
          <div class="loop-step"><span>As requested</span><strong>Fact maintenance</strong><p>Process the included factual changes and correction.</p></div>
          <div class="loop-step"><span>Quarterly</span><strong>Review</strong><p>Review trends, material alerts, and next priorities.</p></div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="section tint">
      <div class="shell">
        <div class="section-head center"><div class="section-kicker">Pricing questions</div><h2 class="section-title">Before you commit.</h2></div>
        <div class="faq-list">
          <details><summary>Is the $495 Snapshot credited toward a Build?</summary><p>Yes. The Snapshot fee can be credited toward a qualifying Infrastructure Build started within 30 days.</p></details>
          <details><summary>Does the Infrastructure Build require Maintenance?</summary><p>The mockup treats the Build as a standalone deliverable. Maintenance is recommended when the underlying facts, sources, or representation need recurring attention.</p></details>
          <details><summary>What falls outside the standard Build?</summary><p>Additional brands, domains, markets, languages, large catalogs, feed integrations, and complex workflows require a custom scope.</p></details>
          <details><summary>What is a “small infrastructure correction”?</summary><p>A contained adjustment to the maintained Truth Profile, machine-readable record, or previously implemented structured data. New templates, integrations, or broad website work are excluded.</p></details>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

